, Qatar, and the United Arab Emirates to the east, Oman to the southeast, and Yemen to the south. The Gulf of Aqaba in the northwest separates it from Egypt and Israel."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q851","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q367825","value_label":"Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud","from_t":2015.0602739726028,"to_t":null,"title":"head of state","property":"P35","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q3692","value_label":"Riyadh","from_t":1819,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Riyadh"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q13955","value_label":"Arabic","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Arabic"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q1034036","value_label":"Saudi Arabic","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Saudi Arabic"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q432","value_label":"Islam","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P3075","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Islam"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"religion","value_qid":"Q432","value_label":"Islam","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P140","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Islam"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q184558","value_label":"absolute monarchy","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P122","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"absolute monarchy"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q138567551","value_label":"islamic theocracy","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P122","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"islamic theocracy"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q7269","value_label":"monarchy","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P122","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"monarchy"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q56885910","value_label":"Emirate of Diriyah","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P155","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Emirate of Diriyah"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q1756546","value_label":"Kingdom of Nejd and Hejaz","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1365","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Kingdom of Nejd and Hejaz"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"flag","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Flag of Saudi Arabia.svg","from_t":1973.2,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P41","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"coat","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Emblem of Saudi Arabia.svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P94","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q151509","value_label":"Ibn Saud","from_t":1932.0382513661202,"to_t":1953.854794520548,"title":"King of Saudi Arabia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Ibn Saud"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q183187","value_label":"Fahd bin Abdulaziz Al Saud","from_t":1982.4465753424658,"to_t":2005.5808219178082,"title":"King of Saudi Arabia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Fahd bin Abdulaziz Al Saud"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q208301","value_label":"Khalid of Saudi Arabia","from_t":1975.227397260274,"to_t":1982.4465753424658,"title":"King of Saudi Arabia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Khalid of Saudi Arabia"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q217167","value_label":"King Faisal bin Abdulaziz Al Saud","from_t":1964.8360655737704,"to_t":1975.227397260274,"title":"King of Saudi Arabia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"King Faisal bin Abdulaziz Al Saud"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q244206","value_label":"Saud of Saudi Arabia","from_t":1953.854794520548,"to_t":1964.8360655737704,"title":"King of Saudi Arabia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Saud of Saudi Arabia"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q57298","value_label":"Abdullah of Saudi Arabia","from_t":2005.5808219178082,"to_t":2015.0602739726028,"title":"King of Saudi Arabia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Abdullah of Saudi Arabia"},{"qid":"Q851","kind":"flag","value_qid":"Q160877","value_label":"Flag of Saudi Arabia.svg","from_t":1973.2,"to_t":null,"title":"flag of Saudi Arabia","property":"P163","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"flag of Saudi Arabia"}],"people":{"Q367825":{"label":"Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud","description":"King of Saudi Arabia since 2015","enwiki":"Salman of Saudi Arabia","summary":"Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud (Arabic: سلمان بن عبد العزيز آل سعود, romanized: Salmān ibn ʻAbd al-ʻAzīz Āl Saʻūd; born 31 December 1935) is King of Saudi Arabia, having reigned since 2015. He is a son of King Abdulaziz, the founder of Saudi Arabia, and a member of the House of Saud.\nSalman is the third-oldest living head of state and the oldest living monarch. He is the first Saudi head of state born after the unification of Saudi Arabia.","image":"الصورة الرسمية لخادم الحرمين الشريفين الملك سلمان بن عبدالعزيز آل سعود.jpg","birth":1935.9972602739726,"death":null},"Q151509":{"label":"Ibn Saud","description":"King of Saudi Arabia from 1932 to 1953","enwiki":"Ibn Saud","summary":"Abdulaziz bin Abdul Rahman bin Faisal Al Saud (Arabic: عَبْدُ الْعَزِيزِ بْنُ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ بْنِ فَيْصَلٍ آلِ سُعُود; 15 January 1876 – 9 November 1953), known in the Western world as Ibn Saud (Arabic: ابن سعود; Ibn Suʿūd), and known with his kunya Abu Turki (Arabic: أَبُو تُرْكِي), was a Najdi war leader, statesman, and religious leader who became the founder and first King of Saudi Arabia, reigning from 23 September 1932 until his death in 1953. He had ruled parts of the kingdom since 1902, having previously been Emir, Sultan, King of Nejd, and King of Hejaz.\nIbn Saud was the son of Abdul Rahman bin Faisal, Emir of Nejd, and Sara bint Ahmed Al Sudairi. The family were exiled from their residence in the city of Riyadh in 1890.","image":"Ibn Saud.png","birth":1876.0382513661202,"death":1953.854794520548},"Q183187":{"label":"Fahd bin Abdulaziz Al Saud","description":"King of Saudi Arabia from 1982 to 2005","enwiki":"Fahd of Saudi Arabia","summary":"Fahd bin Abdulaziz Al Saud (1920, 1921 or 1923 – 1 August 2005) was King and Prime Minister of Saudi Arabia from 13 June 1982 until his death in 2005. Prior to his ascension, he was Crown Prince of Saudi Arabia from 1975 to 1982.\nFahd was the eldest of the Sudairi Seven, the sons of King Abdulaziz by Hassa bint Ahmed Al Sudairi. He served as Minister of Education from 1953 to 1962 during the reign of King Saud.","image":"Fahd of Saudi Arabia Portrait.jpg","birth":1921,"death":2005.5808219178082},"Q208301":{"label":"Khalid of Saudi Arabia","description":"King of Saudi Arabia (1911-1982)","enwiki":"Khalid of Saudi Arabia","summary":"Khalid bin Abdulaziz Al Saud (13 February 1913 – 13 June 1982) was King and Prime Minister of Saudi Arabia from 25 March 1975 until his death in 1982. Before his ascension, he was Crown Prince of Saudi Arabia. Khalid was the sixth son of King Abdulaziz, the founder of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.\nKhalid was the son of King Abdulaziz and Al Jawhara bint Musaed Al Saud.","image":"Khalid II of Saudi Arabia portrait.jpg","birth":1911.1178082191782,"death":1982.4465753424658},"Q217167":{"label":"King Faisal bin Abdulaziz Al Saud","description":"King of Saudi Arabia from 1964 to 1975","enwiki":"Faisal of Saudi Arabia","summary":"Faisal bin Abdulaziz Al Saud (14 April 1906 – 25 March 1975) was King of Saudi Arabia from 1964 until his assassination in 1975. Before his ascension, he served as Crown Prince of Saudi Arabia from 1953 to 1964, and he was briefly regent to his half-brother King Saud in 1964. He was prime minister from 1954 to 1960 and from 1962 to 1975. Faisal was the third son of King Abdulaziz, the founder of modern Saudi Arabia.","image":"King Faisal of Saudi Arabia on on arrival ceremony welcoming 05-27-1971 (cropped).jpg","birth":1906.282191780822,"death":1975.227397260274},"Q244206":{"label":"Saud of Saudi Arabia","description":"King of Saudi Arabia from 1953 to 1964","enwiki":"Saud of Saudi Arabia","summary":"Saud bin Abdulaziz Al Saud (Arabic: سعود بن عبد العزيز آل سعود; 15 January 1902 – 23 February 1969) was King of Saudi Arabia from 9 November 1953 until his abdication on 2 November 1964. During his reign, he served as Prime Minister of Saudi Arabia from 1953 to 1954 and from 1960 to 1962. Prior to his accession, Saud was Crown Prince of Saudi Arabia from 11 May 1933 to 9 November 1953. He was the second son of King Abdulaziz, the founder of Saudi Arabia.","image":"Saud IV of Saudi Arabia portrait.jpg","birth":1902.0383561643835,"death":1969.145205479452},"Q57298":{"label":"Abdullah of Saudi Arabia","description":"King of Saudi Arabia from 2005 to 2015 (1924–2015)","enwiki":"Abdullah of Saudi Arabia","summary":"Abdullah bin Abdulaziz Al Saud (1 August 1924 – 23 January 2015) was King and Prime Minister of Saudi Arabia from 1 August 2005 until his death in 2015. Prior to his accession, he was Crown Prince of Saudi Arabia from 13 June 1982. He was the tenth son of King Abdulaziz, the founder of Saudi Arabia.\nAbdullah was the son of King Abdulaziz and Fahda bint Asi Al Shuraim.","image":"King Abdullah bin Abdul al-Saud January 2007.jpg","birth":1924.5819672131147,"death":2015.0602739726028}},"media":{"Flag of Saudi Arabia.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Flag_of_Saudi_Arabia.svg/330px-Flag_of_Saudi_Arabia.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Saudi_Arabia.svg","author":"The Shura Council","license":"Public domain"},"Emblem of Saudi Arabia.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Emblem_of_Saudi_Arabia.svg/330px-Emblem_of_Saudi_Arabia.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons